Evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

solution_steps:
We can distribute scalar multiplication across projection, so
\[\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} (-2 \mathbf{v}) = -2 \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v}.\]Since $\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix},$
\[-2 \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 0 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}}.\]The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}-2\0\6\end{pmatrix}

