solution_steps:
By the tangent addition formula, we have
\begin{align*}
\arctan \left( \frac{a}{b + c} \right) + \arctan \left( \frac{b}{a + c} \right) &= \arctan \left( \frac{\frac{a}{b+c} + \frac{b}{a+c}}{1 - \frac{a}{b+c} \cdot \frac{b}{a+c}} \right) \\
&= \arctan \left( \frac{a(a+c) + b(b+c)}{(b+c)(a+c) - ab} \right).
\end{align*}
Since angle C is a right angle, we have $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$.
Thus,
\begin{align*}
\arctan \left( \frac{a}{b + c} \right) + \arctan \left( \frac{b}{a + c} \right) &= \arctan \left( \frac{a(a+c) + b(b+c)}{(b+c)(a+c) - ab} \right) \\
&= \arctan \left( \frac{a^2 + ab + b^2 + c(a+b)}{a^2 + ab + b^2 + c(a+b)} \right) \\
&= \arctan 1 \\
&= \boxed{\frac{\pi}{4}}.
\end{align*}The answer is: \frac{\pi}{4}

